<title>USA: US attache ups 96/97 India centrif. sugar forecast.</title>
<headline>US attache ups 96/97 India centrif. sugar forecast.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. Agricultural Department attache estimated India 1996/97 centrifugal sugar production at 16.7 million tonnes, the second highest level ever and up from a previous forecast of 14.1 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The attache said sugarcane production and area are expected to reach the third highest levels on record, helped by one of the best monsoons of the past nine years.</p>
<p>The attache's estimate exceeds the official USDA forecast of 15 million tonnes issued last month in the World Agricultural Production report.</p>
<p>India is forecast to have a record outturn of nearly 18.2 million tonnes in 1995/96.</p>
<p>The attache also said large carry over stocks and lower prices are seen pushing exports in 1996/97 to a record 1.5 million tonnes.</p>
</text>
